  "prefLabel": "Agr 908.07 Permitting of Native Lumber Graders",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 908.07 Permitting of Native Lumber Graders.\n\n(a) In order to receive a native lumber grading permit, the prospective grader shall:\n\n(1) Review the New Hampshire Native Lumber Law Self-Study Booklet, 2016 edition, issued by the university of New Hampshire cooperative extension available as noted in Appendix II, in the subject of grading standards; and\n\n(2) Demonstrate competency by passing the native lumber grading test, pursuant to Agr 908.08.\n\n(b) The native lumber grading permit shall be effective for 5 years, at which time the grader may renew the permit by completing the steps in Agr 908.07(a).\n\n(c) The native lumber grading permit is nontransferable.\n\nSource. #6171, eff 1-24-96, EXPIRED: 1-24-04\n\nNew. #14550, eff 4-1-26, EXPIRES: 4-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr900.html"
